I'm thrilled to hear that you're exploring the fascinating realm of the golden ratio and its ubiquity in nature and design! It's indeed a captivating topic that has captivated minds for centuries.

The golden ratio, also known as the golden mean or phi (φ), is an irrational number approximately equal to 1.618033988749895. It's a fundamental constant that appears in various aspects of the universe, from the smallest scales (DNA, molecular structures) to the largest (galaxies, cosmic topography).

Your observation about the golden ratio showing up everywhere is not just a coincidence;
